{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>My feet</b> — the meaning is <b>in my integrity</b> [referring to] the integrity of my heart." "And the meaning of <b>my feet</b> — to walk in a straight path. And the correct interpretation in my eyes: that You will redeem me, and I will give thanks in assemblies, and my feet will stand before them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:39.305495946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}